Windows: resolve Python bootstrap files from manifest-only runfiles.

When a Python executable is used as an action tool, Bazel may materialize
only the runfiles manifest on Windows. Generated files, including the
rules_python stage-2 bootstrap and the hermetic interpreter, are listed in
that manifest but are not present below the adjacent `.runfiles` directory.
The launcher must resolve those files through the manifest before reporting
them as missing or creating a runtime venv from a non-existent path.

The same lookup is needed for the explicit venv symlinks used on Windows.
Those entries commonly point at individual files in external repositories,
such as `patch_ng.py`; constructing a path below the synthetic runfiles root
would otherwise create a dangling link and leave the dependency unavailable
to the runtime interpreter.

